# LogIQ Advisor - Pipeline Overview

LogIQ Advisor is a three-stage, agent-based log-analysis pipeline. Each stage is a
specialized agent with a strict scope. Deterministic work (parsing, schema validation,
JSON persistence) is done by Python scripts in the `logiq/` package; reasoning, research,
and synthesis are done by the corresponding agent.

## Stages

Each stage is a custom agent in `.cursor/agents/`, invocable with `/<name>`:

1. Log Collector (`logiq-collect`): parse raw logs -> `errors.json`
2. Log Researcher (`logiq-research`): research each error (web + Glean MCP) -> `research.json`
3. Log Synthesizer (`logiq-synthesize`): consolidate -> `resolution.json`

The `/logiq-run` command orchestrates all three in order.

```
logs + app_name --> [Collector] --> errors.json
errors.json      --> [Researcher] --> research.json
errors.json + research.json --> [Synthesizer] --> resolution.json
```

## Application name argument

Every run is scoped to an application. The application name is provided as an input
argument (`--app-name` for the Python CLI, `<app-name>` for the slash commands). It is
written into `errors.json` and propagated through every stage. The Researcher uses it to
build targeted Glean MCP / BMC Helix ITSM queries.

## Input path

The log input path is optional. When omitted it defaults to the repo's `data/input/`
folder (`--input` for the Python CLI). `/logiq-run` takes only `<app-name>` and always
reads from `data/input/`.

## Run directory convention

All artifacts for a single run live under `data/runs/<run_id>/`:

- `data/runs/<run_id>/errors.json` (Collector output)
- `data/runs/<run_id>/research.json` (Researcher output)
- `data/runs/<run_id>/resolution.json` (Synthesizer output, one summary per distinct error)

`run_id` defaults to `<app_name>-<UTC-timestamp>` and is created by the Collector stage.
Always reuse the same `run_id` across the three stages of one run.

Each new Collector run clears `data/runs/` first (deletes all prior run directories)
so only the current run's artifacts remain on disk.

## Data contracts

Defined and validated in `logiq/schemas.py`. All JSON is UTF-8 with `ensure_ascii=False`.

`errors.json`
```json
{
  "run_id": "string",
  "app_name": "string",
  "generated_at": "ISO-8601 UTC",
  "errors": [
    {
      "id": "string",
      "level": "ERROR | WARNING | EXCEPTION | CRITICAL | FATAL",
      "message": "string",
      "timestamp": "string | null",
      "module": "string | null",
      "stack_trace": "string | null",
      "source_file": "string",
      "line_no": 0,
      "context_lines": ["string"]
    }
  ]
}
```

`research.json`
```json
{
  "run_id": "string",
  "app_name": "string",
  "generated_at": "ISO-8601 UTC",
  "findings": [
    {
      "error_id": "string",
      "likely_causes": ["string"],
      "resolutions": ["string"],
      "references": [
        { "type": "web | glean | bmc_helix", "title": "string", "url_or_id": "string" }
      ],
      "confidence": "high | medium | low"
    }
  ]
}
```

`resolution.json`
```json
{
  "run_id": "string",
  "app_name": "string",
  "generated_at": "ISO-8601 UTC",
  "summaries": [
    {
      "error_summary": "string",
      "root_cause": "string",
      "resolution_steps": ["string"],
      "references": [
        { "type": "web | glean | bmc_helix", "title": "string", "url_or_id": "string" }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

One entry per distinct error pattern (duplicate log lines collapsed).

## Separation of concerns

- Collector: reads input logs, writes `errors.json`. No research, no resolutions.
- Researcher: read-only. Reads `errors.json`, researches, writes `research.json`. Never modifies logs, systems, or configs.
- Synthesizer: reads `errors.json` + `research.json`, writes `resolution.json`. No web, no Glean, no DB, no modifications.
